                <pb facs="0563" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1732.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Ciudad Juarez to the Secretary
                        of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad
                                Juarez</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Provisional President Madero and Provisional Governor Gonzales are here, and have
                    set up local government for Juarez. I am acting in harmony with the Government
                    de facto. The provisional governor seems anxious to favor Americans and work in
                    harmony with them in the establishment of law and order.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
